  <p>The walkthrough below matches the actual interface on this page.</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Identify the reference angle <span set:html={rich('[[A]]')} />.</strong> Decide which acute angle the ratio describes, since the opposite side is defined relative to it.</li>
    <li><strong>Locate the hypotenuse <span set:html={rich('[[c]]')} />.</strong> It is the side opposite the right angle and the longest side of the triangle.</li>
    <li><strong>Locate the opposite side <span set:html={rich('[[a]]')} />.</strong> It is the side directly across from angle <span set:html={rich('[[A]]')} />.</li>
    <li><strong>Measure or obtain both side lengths.</strong> Use a tape, a drawing, or given data, keeping the same unit for both.</li>
    <li><strong>Enter the hypotenuse in the first input field.</strong> This is the larger of the two values.</li>
    <li><strong>Enter the opposite side in the second input field.</strong> This is the smaller of the two values.</li>
